{"title":"1961 AHSME Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Non-rigorous)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Non-rigorous)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Two tangents are drawn to a circle from an exterior point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />; they touch the circle at points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> respectively. \nA third tangent intersects segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and touches the circle at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/5/775555f62256a77b1244bfe91ea5b61c033bb476.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=20$\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, then the perimeter of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/6/606f84b88e7c08e0c19d5cb82e2d9af5c0e04971.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$APR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/2/0a2b09aadbf1e308911cdfe5651d99aab20dfc30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 42\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 40.5 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 40\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 39\\frac{7}{8} \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{not determined by the given information}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"699\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:1961_AHSME_Problem_11.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/7/74/1961_AHSME_Problem_11.png/300px-1961_AHSME_Problem_11.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"270\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/7/74/1961_AHSME_Problem_11.png/450px-1961_AHSME_Problem_11.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/7/74/1961_AHSME_Problem_11.png/600px-1961_AHSME_Problem_11.png 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>Draw the diagram as shown.  Note that the two tangent lines from a single outside point of a circle have the exact same length, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/2/ec24d58515a2285308cb9272c583faded5741768.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = AC = 20$\" width=\"122\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/d/f7d102dd61cde843ae016067580eb39fc316f9c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BP = PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"81\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/9/5b94dea58fa69b7ad2f83f7ce6ada35417174655.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QR = CR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"81\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>The perimeter of the triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/d/30dcf61682c10b68ef8c09222f0a3becc130244f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP + PR + AR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"128\" height=\"14\" />.  Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/8/f7841d3dfc0d3cf2becef63f0624495a9d4fc994.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ + QR = PR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"131\" height=\"16\" />, so from substitution, the perimeter is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/d/5fd2b44a5bca7a5f2a1b11ce33eba2a6b30ec050.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AP + PQ + QR + AR\\]\" width=\"178\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/3/e83a9d7d135210ae7da5bd0eff3b3c38ca787750.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AP + BP + CR + AR\\]\" width=\"178\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/f/23f0fec0219ebb0a5460ef26d740c0425a4e3a31.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AB + AC\\]\" width=\"78\" height=\"14\" />\nThus, the perimeter of the triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/f/fffc7368e8e7b77c88b0b4bf732c88c60e27b439.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"42\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Non-rigorous.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Non-rigorous)\">Solution 2 (Non-rigorous)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Non-rigorous)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> can be anywhere on the circle between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, it can basically be \"on top\" of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> will be at the same point as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/6/606f84b88e7c08e0c19d5cb82e2d9af5c0e04971.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$APR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> form a degenerate triable with side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/5/775555f62256a77b1244bfe91ea5b61c033bb476.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=20$\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />. So its perimeter will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/c/30c3000adfce9843a0208f2471abb504ee29d2d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BP=PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/1/921a52986cca54a09dcf5b32dc76a7eb0551b2ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QR=CR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"81\" height=\"16\" /> by power of a point, as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/b/e3bb4eeb347e74e025fd175c22f1f7275af0555e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/1/201e0f38191233f52b0d395bda64be69e9b831b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> decrease in length, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/3/2d34714ba1de520e3634e2cd87a600bea1399b02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PR=PQ+QR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"133\" height=\"18\" /> will \"grow\" to compensate, so the perimeter will stay constant with a value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/8/f689793f71a29a39682fe7101e7c307c13f98fe4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 40}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"64\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>We can also skip verifying that the perimeter will stay constant, since it seems unlikely that MAA would create a question with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/7/f6703a012239be39532a0bea99c3ecb4f4c5574e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{not determined by the given information}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"298\" height=\"17\" /> as the answer.\n</p><p>~jd9\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><i>By Ajeet Dubey | <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://ioqm.in\">ioqm.in</a></i>\n</p><p>Let the third tangent meet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and touch the circle at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />. Tangent segments from the same external point are equal, so\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/2/14209d88bc9d96afdbd986049e3bd88487f83656.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=AC=20,\\qquad PB=PQ,\\qquad RC=RQ.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"375\" height=\"18\" />\nHence\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/b/ebbd2ee437a9e55c0c09ec30db62694c9de89bb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP=20-PQ, \\qquad AR=20-RQ, \\qquad PR=PQ+RQ.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"463\" height=\"18\" />\nThe perimeter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/7/c373eb0aae1ed8ad7d5755eb6f1baeaa1f7cf494.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle APR$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is therefore\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/b/e3bf2c3b7986c32a50dc8f41a7c1aa1f2f3ee88a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP+AR+PR=(20-PQ)+(20-RQ)+(PQ+RQ)=40.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"505\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Thus the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/f/fffc7368e8e7b77c88b0b4bf732c88c60e27b439.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"42\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME\" title=\"1961 AHSME\">1961 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1961 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1961 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1961\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1961 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1961 AHSME Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1961 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1961 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1961 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1961 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1961 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1961 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index